📘
  🎈 Deflate: bytes in, a gzip stream out. The package knows nothing of HTTP.

    🤐🐇🎈 data❗️ ➡️ stream         💭 what `gzip -dc` turns back into data
    🧾🐇🎈 data❗️ ➡️ checksum       💭 the CRC-32 that such a stream ends with

  The README says what a stream is made of.
📘

📜 🔤../shared/bytes.🍇🔤

💭 Deflate packs its codes into bytes from the lowest bit up. This takes values of any
💭 width, lowest bit first, and keeps whole bytes as they fill.
